I am interested in inputting my own environmental variable rasters into Wallace to look at vegetation distribution in Southern California. The rasters are currently all in NAD 83 California Teale Albers, which uses meters for the units. If I have all the raster layers in the same extent, cell size, and projection am I good to go?

Do you have any other tips for using user-defined rasters for the environmental variables to make it smoother?

Thank you!

On Tuesday, July 31, 2018 at 7:29:29 AM UTC-7, Jamie M. Kass wrote:
> Huy is right, you will just need to make sure that your rasters are in the same projection. And also be aware that the buffer units are in the same units as your coordinate reference system, which means that if you input UTM data you will need to enter 10000 for a 10 km buffer.
>
> We’re working right now on better functionality for testing raster projections that are input by users, and we’ll keep you updated on any progress.
>
> Jamie

